From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Paslawski <chris@paslawski.me>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 21:49:35 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] ipa: simple: Honour frame duration limits

Expose frame duration limits from the sensor timing controls and apply
both ends of a request through VBLANK. Limiting exposure alone does not
limit the frame rate, and fixed-rate requests need longer frames even
when the scene is bright. Keep the sensor's minimum blanking and reserve
its exposure margin when changing the frame length.

Restore native blanking and refresh the exposure range before configuring
the software IPA. Reopening the same sensor mode must not derive its
exposure margin from a previous session's stretched frame length.

Report the frame duration from the controls applied to the captured
frame, rather than echoing the requested rate.

The optional maxFrameTime tuning key caps long exposures in dim light.
With stretchGain, raise gain to that value before lengthening exposure
past the sensor's native frame. Neither tuning key is required to honour
requested frame duration limits.

